	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&mtc-cnstr;NativeUnitEnum_GRAVITATIONALACCELERATION">
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="&mtc-cnstr;NativeUnitEnum"/>
		<rdfs:label rdf:datatype="&xs;string">GRAVITATIONAL_ACCELERATION</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://model.mtconnect.org/ontology/machinetool/DataTypes/"/>
		<iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition rdf:datatype="&xs;string">acceleration relative to earth&apos;s gravity given in meter per second squared.

&gt; Note 1 to entry: At different points on Earth&apos;s surface, the free-fall acceleration ranges from 9.764 to 9.834 m/s2 (Wikipedia: Gravitational Acceleration). The constant can be customized depending on the location in the universe.

&gt; Note 2 to entry: In the standard, it is assumed that Earth&apos;s average value of gravitational acceleration is 9.90665 m/s2.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="&mtc-cnstr;NativeUnitEnum_GRAVITATIONALFORCE">
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="&mtc-cnstr;NativeUnitEnum"/>
